{"id":"38339d60720b0f2a","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal.md","title":"ZFC Largecard4 N Huge Cardinal","display":"df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal — ZFC Largecard4 N Huge Cardinal","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal","aliases":["58-df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal"],"display":"df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal — ZFC Largecard4 N Huge Cardinal","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-class-embedding-data.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-largecard4-n-huge-cardinal — ZFC Largecard4 N Huge Cardinal"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5578254565969219\" href=\"?note=5578254565969219\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-class-embedding-data.md\">../batch04/58-df-class-embedding-data.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\\in V\">\\(\\kappa\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> ranges over transitive classes and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"j:V\\to M\">\\(j:V\\to M\\)</span> over class functions in the ambient class metatheory</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> (cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{class}\">\\(\\mathrm{class}\\)</span> (sort marker on the metatheoretic class quantifier <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists^{\\mathrm{class}}\">\\(\\exists^{\\mathrm{class}}\\)</span>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClassElemEmb}_S(j,M)\">\\(\\mathrm{ClassElemEmb}_S(j,M)\\)</span> (class-elementarity schema defined below)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SeqClosedClass}_S(M,\\lambda)\">\\(\\mathrm{SeqClosedClass}_S(M,\\lambda)\\)</span> (closure under set-coded <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span>-sequences, defined below)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcLargecard4NHugeCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcLargecard4NHugeCardinal}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>外部接口 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClassCriticalPoint}\">\\(\\mathrm{ClassCriticalPoint}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}\">\\(\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitiveClass}\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitiveClass}\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"5578254565969219\" href=\"?note=5578254565969219\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-class-embedding-data.md\">../batch04/58-df-class-embedding-data.md</a> 的同名定义与参数次序。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{meta}\">\\(\\mathrm{meta}\\)</span> 为本原子在下式引入、量化绑定或仅作层级/排版标签的记号；其参数次序与适用域由相应公式固定，不作为额外的未声明外部对象。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClassElemEmb}_S(j,M)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{TransitiveClass}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(M)\n\\land\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,V,M).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ClassElemEmb}_S(j,M)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{TransitiveClass}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(M)\n\\land\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(j,V,M).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SeqClosedClass}_S(M,\\lambda)\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,\\lambda,\\operatorname{ran}(f))\\land\\operatorname{ran}(f)\\subseteq M\n\\to f\\in M\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{SeqClosedClass}_S(M,\\lambda)\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,\\lambda,\\operatorname{ran}(f))\\land\\operatorname{ran}(f)\\subseteq M\n\\to f\\in M\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{ZfcLargecard4NHugeCardinal}_S(\\kappa,n)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land n\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists^{\\mathrm{class}}M,j\\;\\exists s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ClassElemEmb}_S(j,M)\\land\\mathrm{ClassCriticalPoint}_{58}(\\kappa,j)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(s,n+1,\\operatorname{ran}(s))\\land s(0)=\\kappa\n\\land\\forall m\\in n\\;(s(m+1)=j(s(m)))\n\\land\\mathrm{SeqClosedClass}_S(M,s(n))\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{ZfcLargecard4NHugeCardinal}_S(\\kappa,n)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land n\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists^{\\mathrm{class}}M,j\\;\\exists s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ClassElemEmb}_S(j,M)\\land\\mathrm{ClassCriticalPoint}_{58}(\\kappa,j)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(s,n+1,\\operatorname{ran}(s))\\land s(0)=\\kappa\n\\land\\forall m\\in n\\;(s(m+1)=j(s(m)))\n\\land\\mathrm{SeqClosedClass}_S(M,s(n))\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=1\">\\(n=1\\)</span> the closure length is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"j(\\kappa)\">\\(j(\\kappa)\\)</span>, giving the usual huge-cardinal condition; higher <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> use the finite iterate sequence <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s\">\\(s\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The critical-point clause is expanded as “<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"j\">\\(j\\)</span> fixes every ordinal below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> and moves <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>”; no undeclared <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{crit}\">\\(\\operatorname{crit}\\)</span> operator is used. The iterate code <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s\">\\(s\\)</span> is required to be a function, not merely a relation with the right domain.</li>\n<li>The two class predicates and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists^{\\mathrm{class}}\">\\(\\exists^{\\mathrm{class}}\\)</span> belong to the stated ambient class metatheory. They are not mis-typed as set quantifiers of first-order ZFC.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-class-embedding-data.md","status":"resolved","id":"5578254565969219","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excer